# Quark - Self-Hosted Media Streaming Server

Quark is a self-hosted media streaming server built with Python 3.12 and FastAPI, focused on original quality playback, adaptive HLS streaming, and rich metadata.

## Features

- **Direct Play** via HTTP Byte Range requests
- **Adaptive HLS streaming** with live transcoding fallback
- **Optimization queue** for pre-encoded HLS renditions (2160p to 144p)
- **Metadata** via TMDB, artwork via FanArt.tv, subtitles via OpenSubtitles
- **JSON-based storage** (no SQL database)
- **Cross-platform** (Windows + Linux)

## Quick Start

```bash
# Windows
python -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Linux
python3.12 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Configuration

1. Edit `.env` (or copy from `.env.example`) — add API keys for TMDB, FanArt.tv, OpenSubtitles
2. Edit `config/libraries.json` — add media library paths

## Media Folder Structure

Movies and TV shows live in separate folders:

```
media/
├── movies/                        # Movies — any filename
│   └── Big_Buck_Bunny_2008_720p.mp4
└── tvshows/                       # TV shows — strict structure
    └── Breaking Bad/              # Folder named after the show (TMDB search term)
        ├── S01/                   # Season folders: S01, S02, ... or "Season 01"
        │   ├── ep1.mp4            # Any episode file — only the episode number matters
        │   ├── EP02.mp4
        │   └── episode03.mkv
        └── S02/
            └── episode01.mp4
```

**TV rules:**
- `tvshows/<Show Name>/<S##>/<episode files>` — exactly this structure
- Season folders: `S01`, `S02`, `Season 01`, `season_1`
- Episode numbers are detected from filenames: `ep1`, `EP01`, `episode3`, `01x01`, `1x02`, `S01E01`
- The show folder name is used to search TMDB
- After metadata lookup, files are renamed to `01x01 - Pilot.mp4`
  (the episode name comes from TMDB)

## Running

```bash
python run.py
```

The server starts at `http://127.0.0.1:8090` and serves the web UI at the root.

## Web UI

Quark ships with a built-in React web client (in `web/`).

**Dev mode** (hot reload on `http://127.0.0.1:5173`):

```bash
cd web
npm install
npm run dev
```

**Production build** (served by the backend at `/`):

```bash
cd web
npm run build
```

The UI includes:
- Movie and TV show browsing with poster grids and detail pages
- Custom right-click context menu (replaces the browser menu) — Play, Optimize, Refresh metadata, Download subtitles, Mark watched, Remove
- Full-screen player with Direct / HLS / Transcode mode switching
- Watch progress & "mark as watched" tracking
- Plex-style settings page: server, libraries, streaming, optimization, providers

## API Endpoints

| Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|
| `GET /api/system/health` | Health check |
| `GET /api/system/settings` | Get settings (API keys masked) |
| `PUT /api/system/settings` | Save settings (`***` keeps existing key) |
| `POST /api/system/settings/reload` | Reload settings from disk |
| `GET /api/libraries` | List libraries |
| `POST /api/libraries` | Add library |
| `DELETE /api/libraries/{id}` | Remove library |
| `POST /api/libraries/{id}/scan` | Scan library |
| `GET /api/items` | List media items |
| `GET /api/items/{id}` | Item detail + metadata |
| `GET /api/items/{id}/stream` | Stream item (auto/direct/hls/transcode) |
| `GET /api/items/{id}/hls/master.m3u8` | HLS master playlist |
| `POST /api/items/{id}/optimize` | Queue for HLS optimization |
| `GET /api/items/{id}/artwork/{type}` | Get artwork |
| `GET /api/items/{id}/subtitles` | List subtitles |
| `GET /api/state/{id}` | Watch progress / watched state |
| `POST /api/state/{id}/watch` | Mark watched/unwatched |
| `POST /api/state/{id}/progress` | Save playback position |
| `WS /ws` | Real-time event stream |

## Project Structure

```
quark/
├── app/
│   ├── api/          # REST API routes
│   ├── scanner/      # Library scanner
│   ├── metadata/     # Metadata builder
│   ├── artwork/      # Artwork downloader
│   ├── subtitles/    # Subtitle manager
│   ├── media/        # Media detection & probing
│   ├── streaming/    # Byte range + HLS streaming
│   ├── optimization/ # HLS optimization queue
│   ├── transcoding/  # FFmpeg process management
│   ├── providers/    # TMDB, FanArt, OpenSubtitles
│   ├── services/     # Business logic services
│   ├── workers/      # Background workers
│   ├── cache/        # Cache management
│   ├── config/       # Settings & libraries
│   ├── system/       # Platform detection & binaries
│   ├── utils/        # Logging, JSON, hashing, filenames
│   ├── websocket/    # WebSocket manager
│   ├── events/       # Event bus
│   └── main.py       # App entry point
├── config/           # Configuration files
├── media/            # Media library root
├── cache/            # Cache directory
├── docs/             # Documentation
├── logs/             # Log files
└── tests/            # Test suite
```

## External Dependencies

- **FFmpeg** (includes FFprobe) — must be on PATH
- **MediaInfo CLI** — optional, enhances media probing
